  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Programming EU Anti-corruption Initiative In Ukranie</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To complete the assignment, the consultant is expected to lead the formulation of the documents. The consultant will:
&#x2022; Assess updated documentation from partners and context.
&#x2022; Engage in dialogue with EUACI, MFA and EU on content of addendum documents.
&#x2022; Ensure synergies with other relevant MFA supported programmes and projects in line with the &#x201c;Doing Development Differently&#x201d; approach. This includes the global programme on anti-corruption currently being formulated.  
&#x2022; Consult with other relevant stakeholders and programs as needed.
&#x2022; Ensure that the basis for the EUACI will not become too complex and that it is implementable and sustainable with a high impact given the context.
&#x2022; Ensure that the EUACI will have sufficient flexibility and be able to adapt to developments given the unstable context in line with the MFA adaptive management approach.  
&#x2022; Incorporate the four thematic issues across the work of the program.
&#x2022; Incorporate the extensive work on legislative and political development.
&#x2022; Consider aspects of terminating the program in July 2024 and lay out possible tracks for an extension.
&#x2022; Together with EUACI consult partners virtually for a first drafting of engagement document on advance of mission to Kyiv
&#x2022; Draft first version of documents with partners</narrative>
  </description>
